---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

// Pull the latest 3 published blog posts for the homepage teaser.
const latestPosts = (await getCollection('blog', ({ data }) => !data.draft))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf())
  .slice(0, 3);

const blogDateFmt = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', {
  year: 'numeric',
  month: 'short',
  day: 'numeric',
});
---

<Layout
  title="Nocturnus.AI - Reasoning Engine for AI Agents"
  description="Open-source logic engine for AI agents. Deterministic inference, truth maintenance, and salience-ranked context — cutting prompt tokens by 97%."
>
  <Navbar />

  <main>
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- HERO — Dark premium hero with amber accents                       -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="hero-dark" id="top">
      <div class="hero-split">
        <div class="hero-split-left">
          <div class="hero-dark-kicker">CONTEXT SERVER FOR AI AGENTS</div>
          <h1 class="hero-dark-headline">
            Send <span class="hero-accent">30 tokens</span>
            instead of 2,400.
          </h1>
          <p class="hero-dark-sub">
            NocturnusAI sits between your agent and the LLM. It extracts facts, reasons about what's relevant, and returns only what changed.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-cost-line">
            <span class="hero-cost-new">$240<span style="font-weight: 400; font-size: 0.6em; opacity: 0.6;">/mo</span></span>
            <span class="hero-cost-vs">instead of</span>
            <span class="hero-cost-old">$54,000<span style="font-weight: 400; font-size: 0.6em; opacity: 0.5;">/mo</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-dark-ctas">
            <a href="#try-it" class="hero-btn-primary">Try it now</a>
            <a href={`${base}/docs`} class="hero-btn-secondary">Read the docs</a>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-dark-stats">
            <span>97% fewer tokens</span>
            <span class="hero-stat-dot">&middot;</span>
            <span>open source</span>
            <span class="hero-stat-dot">&middot;</span>
            <span>single container</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-split-right">
          <div class="hero-terminal-light">
            <div class="hero-tl-bar">
              <span class="hero-tl-dot" style="background: #FF5F57;"></span>
              <span class="hero-tl-dot" style="background: #FFBD2E;"></span>
              <span class="hero-tl-dot" style="background: #28C840;"></span>
              <span class="hero-tl-label">POST /context</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="hero-tl-code"><span class="htl-comment"># Send raw conversation turns</span>
$ curl localhost:<span class="htl-num">9300</span>/context \
  -d <span class="htl-str">'&#123;
    "turns": [
      "User: login broken after Okta cutover",
      "Tool crm: account=acme tier=enterprise"
    ],
    "sessionId": "ticket-42"
  &#125;'</span>

<span class="htl-comment"># NocturnusAI returns only the delta</span>
<span class="htl-ok">&#10003;</span> <span class="htl-key">briefingDelta</span>: <span class="htl-str">"Login failing post-Okta
  cutover. Acme is enterprise tier."</span>

  <span class="htl-accent">~30 tokens</span> <span class="htl-muted">instead of ~2,400</span></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- WHY NOW — the urgency and the inflection                           -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="site-section-tight" id="why-now">
      <div class="site-container">
        <div class="section-head reveal">
          <div class="site-kicker">Why Now</div>
          <h2 class="site-title" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);">The context layer is happening. The bill already did.</h2>
          <p class="site-subtitle">Three things hit production at the same time — and they all compound. A context server is no longer a nice-to-have; it's the layer the agent stack has been missing.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-grid reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-5);">
          <div class="plain-card" style="border-top: 2px solid var(--site-accent);">
            <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--site-accent); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Cost</div>
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Agent bills scale exponentially, not linearly.</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--site-muted);">A $500 POC becomes $847k/month without changing a single line of code &mdash; just by adding users. Most of those tokens are the model re-reading what it already knows. That's a structural problem, not a tuning problem.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="plain-card" style="border-top: 2px solid var(--site-accent);">
            <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--site-accent); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Correctness</div>
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Similarity is not truth.</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--site-muted);">When an agent decides based on the current state of a record, a clause, or an inventory level, &ldquo;the most semantically similar document&rdquo; is the wrong abstraction. Vector retrieval cannot fix operational hallucinations. Inference over facts can.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="plain-card" style="border-top: 2px solid var(--site-accent);">
            <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--site-accent); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Latency</div>
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Every prompt token is an attention cost.</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--site-muted);">Long-running agents get slower in proportion to their context. Smaller context = faster response. We see 3&times; to 10&times; latency improvements on agents that used to drag as threads grew.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal reveal-delay-2" style="max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--space-4); background: var(--site-surface); border: 1px solid var(--site-line); border-radius: var(--radius-sm);">
          <p style="margin: 0 0 0.8rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;">
            There is going to be a context infrastructure layer in the agent stack &mdash; the same way there is a vector database layer, an orchestration layer, and a model layer. Within 18 months it will be obvious it was always there.
          </p>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--site-muted);">
            Model providers won't build this; they get paid by the token. Agent frameworks won't build this; they need to stay provider-neutral. It's going to be its own layer.
            <a href={`${base}/blog/stop-sending-the-model-what-it-already-knows/`} style="color: var(--site-accent); font-weight: 500;">Read the launch post &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="section-rule" />

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- HOW IT COMPRESSES — reasoning is the mechanism, context is result  -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="site-section-tight" id="compare">
      <div class="site-container">
        <div class="section-head reveal">
          <div class="site-kicker">How It Compresses</div>
          <h2 class="site-title" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);">Reasoning is how you get 97% compression.</h2>
          <p class="site-subtitle">Vector stores retrieve everything that looks vaguely related &mdash; so your context window fills with noise. NocturnusAI uses logical inference to keep only what must be true. That's the difference between ~2,400 tokens and ~30.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- 3-card mechanism: how reasoning → compression → savings -->
        <div class="feature-grid reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">
          <div class="plain-card" style="border-top: 2px solid var(--site-accent);">
            <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--site-accent); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Step 1</div>
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Extracts facts, not chunks</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--site-muted);">The LLM pulls structured predicates from raw turns. No embeddings, no chunks, no similarity matching. Just clean facts: <code>customer_tier(acme, enterprise)</code>.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="plain-card" style="border-top: 2px solid var(--site-accent);">
            <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--site-accent); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Step 2</div>
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Infers what's relevant</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--site-muted);">Backward chaining finds only facts reachable from your agent's current goals. Everything else stays out of the context window. This is why it's 97%, not 30%.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="plain-card" style="border-top: 2px solid var(--site-accent);">
            <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--site-accent); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Step 3</div>
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Returns only the delta</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--site-muted);">Each turn returns a <code>briefingDelta</code> &mdash; what changed since last time. On turn 10, your model sees 30 tokens instead of the full 2,400-token thread replay.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Compact feature bar: the engineering details -->
        <div class="reveal reveal-delay-2" style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2); justify-content: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">
          <span style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; background: var(--site-surface); border: 1px solid var(--site-line); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--site-muted);">
            <strong style="color: var(--site-text);">No LLM required</strong> for inference
          </span>
          <span style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; background: var(--site-surface); border: 1px solid var(--site-line); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--site-muted);">
            <strong style="color: var(--site-text);">1 container</strong> &mdash; no Postgres, Redis, or vector DB
          </span>
          <span style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; background: var(--site-surface); border: 1px solid var(--site-line); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--site-muted);">
            <strong style="color: var(--site-text);">ACID transactions</strong> with truth maintenance
          </span>
          <span style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; background: var(--site-surface); border: 1px solid var(--site-line); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--site-muted);">
            <strong style="color: var(--site-text);">Fork/diff/merge</strong> for hypothetical reasoning
          </span>
        </div>

        <!-- Comparison table: reframed around context outcomes -->
        <div class="section-head reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">
          <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 0;">Why not Mem0, Zep, or Letta?</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--site-muted); margin-top: 0.4rem;">They store and retrieve. NocturnusAI reasons and compresses.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal reveal-delay-3" style="overflow-x: auto;">
          <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.85rem;">
            <thead>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 2px solid var(--site-line);">
                <th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-weight: 600;"></th>
                <th style="text-align: center; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--site-accent);">NocturnusAI</th>
                <th style="text-align: center; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--site-muted);">Mem0</th>
                <th style="text-align: center; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--site-muted);">Zep</th>
                <th style="text-align: center; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--site-muted);">Letta</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--site-line);">
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 1rem;">Context strategy</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-accent); font-weight: 600;">Goal-driven inference</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">Similarity search</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">Graph retrieval</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">Agent-managed</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--site-line);">
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 1rem;">Compression method</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-accent); font-weight: 600;">briefingDelta (only what changed)</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">&mdash;</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">Summarization</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">Compaction</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--site-line);">
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 1rem;">Works without LLM</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-accent); font-weight: 600;">Yes &mdash; inference is deterministic</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">No</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">No</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">No</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--site-line);">
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 1rem;">Self-hosted complexity</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-accent); font-weight: 600;">1 container, 1 port</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">3 containers</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">Graph DB required</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">DB required</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--site-line);">
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 1rem;">MCP tools</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-accent); font-weight: 600;">16 tools</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">9 tools</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">Experimental</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">Consumer only</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 1rem;">Framework integrations</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-accent); font-weight: 600;">8</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">4</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">2</td>
                <td style="text-align: center; padding: 0.6rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">2</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="reveal reveal-delay-3" style="text-align: center; margin-top: var(--space-4); font-size: 0.88rem;">
          <a href={`${base}/how-it-works`} style="color: var(--site-accent); font-weight: 500;">How the logic engine compresses context &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="section-rule" />

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- THE NUMBERS — cost proof                                          -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="site-section-tight" id="numbers">
      <div class="site-container">
        <div class="section-head reveal">
          <div class="site-kicker">The Cost</div>
          <h2 class="site-title" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.1rem);">$240/month instead of $54,000.</h2>
          <p class="site-subtitle">At 1,000 requests/hour on GPT-4o. The ratio holds across providers.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal reveal-delay-1" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); margin-bottom: var(--space-5);">
          <div class="plain-card" style="text-align: center; padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-3);">
            <div style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--site-accent); line-height: 1;">~30</div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--site-muted); margin-top: 0.5rem;">tokens per turn</div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft); margin-top: 0.25rem;">with NocturnusAI</div>
          </div>
          <div class="plain-card" style="text-align: center; padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-3); opacity: 0.35;">
            <div style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono); line-height: 1;">~2,400</div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--site-muted); margin-top: 0.5rem;">tokens per turn</div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft); margin-top: 0.25rem;">full replay</div>
          </div>
          <div class="plain-card" style="text-align: center; padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-3);">
            <div style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--site-accent); line-height: 1;">97%</div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--site-muted); margin-top: 0.5rem;">reduction</div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft); margin-top: 0.25rem;">per request</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- How we calculated this -->
        <div class="reveal reveal-delay-2" style="max-width: 740px; margin: 0 auto;">
          <div class="plain-card" style="padding: var(--space-4); border-left: 3px solid var(--site-accent);">
            <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 0.8rem;">How we calculated this</h3>
            <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--space-3); font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.72; color: var(--site-muted);">
              <div>
                <strong style="color: var(--site-text); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">Without NocturnusAI</strong>
                A 10-turn support conversation averages ~2,400 input tokens per LLM call when replaying the full thread (user messages, tool outputs, system events). At 1,000 requests/hour on GPT-4o ($15/1M input tokens), that's <strong style="color: var(--site-text);">$54,000/month</strong>.
              </div>
              <div>
                <strong style="color: var(--site-text); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">With NocturnusAI</strong>
                The <code>briefingDelta</code> returns only new facts since the last turn &mdash; typically 20&ndash;40 tokens. Same scenario: <strong style="color: var(--site-text);">$240/month</strong>. The logic engine runs locally with zero token cost. Only the initial LLM extraction step uses tokens.
              </div>
            </div>
            <p style="margin-top: var(--space-2); font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--site-muted-soft);">
              Calculation: 1,000 req/hr &times; 720 hr/mo &times; token cost. Claude, Gemini, and local Ollama cost less per token but the compression ratio (30 vs 2,400) is the same regardless of provider. The 97% figure is (2,400 &minus; 30) / 2,400.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="section-rule" />

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- TRY IT — zero-friction first value                                -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="site-section" id="try-it">
      <div class="site-container">
        <div class="section-head reveal">
          <div class="site-kicker">Try It</div>
          <h2 class="site-title" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.1rem);">Running in 10 seconds. No API keys.</h2>
          <p class="site-subtitle">
            The logic engine, fact storage, inference, and context ranking all work instantly. Add an LLM later for natural-language extraction.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Quick-start TL;DR -->
        <div class="reveal" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-5);">
          <div class="panel-dark" style="padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4); border-top: 2px solid var(--site-accent);">
            <div class="panel-label">Fastest path &mdash; 3 lines, no signup</div>
            <pre style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.9; white-space: pre-wrap;">docker run -d --name nocturnusai -p 9300:9300 ghcr.io/auctalis/nocturnusai:latest
curl -s -X POST localhost:9300/tell -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "X-Tenant-ID: default" -d '&#123;"predicate":"likes","args":["alice","logic"]&#125;'
curl -s -X POST localhost:9300/ask  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "X-Tenant-ID: default" -d '&#123;"predicate":"likes","args":["alice","?what"]&#125;'
<span style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.45);"># &rarr; likes(alice, logic)  &mdash; deterministic, sub-millisecond, zero token cost</span></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 1: Store facts, run inference — works instantly -->
        <div class="walkthrough-step reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div class="step-marker">
            <span class="step-number">1</span>
            <span class="step-label">Store facts and run inference &mdash; instant, no LLM</span>
          </div>

          <div class="panel-dark" style="padding: var(--space-4); margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">
            <div class="panel-label">Copy this</div>
            <pre style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.7; white-space: pre-wrap;"><span style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.45);"># Store facts</span>
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:9300/tell \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-Tenant-ID: default" \
  -d '&#123;"predicate":"customer_tier","args":["acme_corp","enterprise"]&#125;'

curl -s -X POST http://localhost:9300/tell \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-Tenant-ID: default" \
